vertical-align:baseline;}<\/style>\n<h2 class=\"kt-adv-heading913_93eda9-b1 wp-block-kadence-advancedheading has-theme-palette-3-color has-text-color\" data-kb-block=\"kb-adv-heading913_93eda9-b1\">AML &amp; KYC DIRECTIVE (Compliance Policy)<\/h2>\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n<\/div><\/div><style>.kb-row-layout-id913_42d844-ba > .kt-row-column-wrap{align-content:start;}:where(.kb-row-layout-id913_42d844-ba > .kt-row-column-wrap) > .wp-block-kadence-column{justify-content:start;}.kb-row-layout-id913_42d844-ba > .kt-row-column-wrap{column-gap:var(--global-kb-gap-md, 2rem);row-gap:var(--global-kb-gap-md, 2rem);max-width:var( --global-content-width, 1290px );padding-left:var(--global-content-edge-padding);padding-right:var(--global-content-edge-padding);padding-top:var(--global-kb-spacing-sm, 1.5rem);padding-bottom:var(--global-kb-spacing-sm, 1.5rem);grid-template-columns:minmax(0, 1fr);}.kb-row-layout-id913_42d844-ba > .kt-row-layout-overlay{opacity:0.30;}@media all and (max-width: 1024px){.kb-row-layout-id913_42d844-ba > .kt-row-column-wrap{grid-template-columns:minmax(0, 1fr);}}@media all and (max-width: 767px){.kb-row-layout-id913_42d844-ba > .kt-row-column-wrap{grid-template-columns:minmax(0, 1fr);}}<\/style><div class=\"kb-row-layout-wrap kb-row-layout-id913_42d844-ba alignnone wp-block-kadence-rowlayout\"><div class=\"kt-row-column-wrap kt-has-1-columns kt-row-layout-equal kt-tab-layout-inherit kt-mobile-layout-row kt-row-valign-top kb-theme-content-width\">\n<style>.kadence-column913_9694b1-78 > .kt-inside-inner-col,.kadence-column913_9694b1-78 > .kt-inside-inner-col:before{border-top-left-radius:0px;border-top-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-right-radius:0px;border-bottom-left-radius:0px;}.kadence-column913_9694b1-78 > .kt-inside-inner-col{column-gap:var(--global-kb-gap-sm, 1rem);}.kadence-column913_9694b1-78 > .kt-inside-inner-col{flex-direction:column;}.kadence-column913_9694b1-78 > .kt-inside-inner-col > .aligncenter{width:100%;}.kadence-column913_9694b1-78 > .kt-inside-inner-col:before{opacity:0.3;}.kadence-column913_9694b1-78{position:relative;}@media all and (max-width: 1024px){.kadence-column913_9694b1-78 > .kt-inside-inner-col{flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;}}@media all and (max-width: 767px){.kadence-column913_9694b1-78 > .kt-inside-inner-col{flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;}}<\/style>\n<div class=\"wp-block-kadence-column kadence-column913_9694b1-78\"><div class=\"kt-inside-inner-col\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Valid from:<\/strong> 12.01.2026 <strong>Company:<\/strong> Bullion Portfolio Trading LLC<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>1. introduction and commitment<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Bullion Portfolio Trading LLC (hereinafter &#8220;the Company&#8221;) does not condone any activity related to money laundering or terrorist financing. As Dubai-based Dealers in Precious Metals and Stones (DPMS), we are committed to maintaining the highest standards in identifying our clients and monitoring transactions. <\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We work with the specialized third-party provider <strong>iDenfy (idenfy.com)<\/strong> to ensure automated, secure and seamless identity verification in real time.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>2. legal basis<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This policy is based on the applicable laws of the United Arab Emirates, in particular:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Federal Decree-Law No. (20) of 2018<\/strong> on combating money laundering and terrorist financing.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Cabinet Decision No. (10) of 2019<\/strong> (implementing provisions).<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Guidelines of the Ministry of Economy for DNFBPs (Designated Non-Financial Businesses and Professions).<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>3. identity verification (KYC) by iDenfy<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">To prevent fraud and identity theft, we use <strong>iDenfy<\/strong> technology for our onboarding process.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>3.1 The digital verification process<\/strong> Customers whose transactions exceed certain thresholds or are classified as high-risk by the system receive a secure link for identification. The process via iDenfy includes: <\/p>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Document verification:<\/strong> The customer scans\/photographs their valid passport or ID card. iDenfy checks the document for security features, holograms and tampering. <\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Biometric facial recognition (Liveness Check):<\/strong> The customer performs a 3D liveness check (selfie scan). The software ensures that the person is physically present (no use of photos, masks or deepfakes). <\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Comparison:<\/strong> The face on the selfie is biometrically compared with the photo on the ID document.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>3.2 Data protection during the check<\/strong> The transmission of data to iDenfy is SSL-encrypted. iDenfy acts as a data processor in accordance with the applicable data protection laws and does not store any data for its own purposes. <\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>4. AML screening and sanction lists<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Parallel to the identity check, the company carries out an automated background check via the iDenfy interface. Customer data is compared with: <\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Global sanctions lists<\/strong> (e.g. UN Security Council, OFAC, EU lists).<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Local UAE Terrorist Lists<\/strong> (UAE Local Terrorist List).<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>PEP lists<\/strong> (Politically Exposed Persons).<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Lists of known fraudsters and wanted persons (Interpol etc.).<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If there is a match in one of these lists, the transaction is automatically put on hold and manually checked by our Compliance Officer.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>5. risk-based approach<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We categorize customer relationships based on risk factors:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Standard Due Diligence (CDD):<\/strong> Used for normal transactions. Requires: Verified ID + selfie via iDenfy. <\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Enhanced Due Diligence (EDD) &#8211; Extended audit:<\/strong> Application for:\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Transactions over <strong>AED 55,000<\/strong> (approx. USD 15,000).<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Politically exposed persons (PEPs).<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Customers from high-risk countries (according to the FATF list).<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Suspicious circumstances.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Additional requirements for EDD:<\/strong> For EDD, customers must provide <strong>proof of the source of funds (<\/strong> e.g. bank statement, payslip, sales certificate).<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>6. monitoring and reporting<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The company constantly monitors transactions for unusual patterns (e.g. &#8220;smurfing&#8221; &#8211; splitting large amounts into small sums in order to circumvent limits).<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We are legally obliged to act in the event of reasonable suspicion of money laundering or illegal activities:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Freeze the transaction immediately.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Submit a<strong>Suspicious Transaction Report (STR<\/strong>) to the UAE Financial Intelligence Unit (FIU) via the <strong>goAML portal<\/strong>.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Not<\/strong> to warn the customer (&#8220;no tipping-off&#8221; rule).<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>7. retention of records<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">All KYC reports (including the results of the iDenfy check, copies of IDs and risk assessments) and transaction documents are securely archived electronically for a period of <strong>at least 5 years<\/strong> after the end of the business relationship.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>8. contact Compliance<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you have any questions about this policy or identity verification, please contact:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Compliance Officer<\/strong> Janko Williams E-Mail: compliance@btp-shop.com<\/p>\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n<\/div><\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>AML &amp; KYC DIRECTIVE (Compliance Policy) Valid from: 12.01.2026 Company: Bullion Portfolio Trading LLC 1. introduction and commitment Bullion Portfolio Trading LLC (hereinafter &#8220;the Company&#8221;) does not condone any activity related to money laundering or terrorist financing. As Dubai-based Dealers in Precious Metals and Stones (DPMS), we are committed to maintaining the highest standards in&#8230;<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"parent":0,"menu_order":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","template":"","meta":{"_seopress_titles_title":"","_seopress_titles_desc":"","_seopress_robots_index":"","_seopress_robots_follow":"","_seopress_robots_imageindex":"","_seopress_robots_snippet":"","_seopress_robots_primary_cat":"","_seopress_robots_breadcrumbs":"","_seopress_robots_freeze_modified_date":"","_seopress_robots_custom_modified_date":"","_seopress_robots_canonical":"","_seopress_social_fb_title":"","_seopress_social_fb_desc":"","_seopress_social_fb_img":"","_seopress_social_fb_img_attachment_id":0,"_seopress_social_fb_img_width":0,"_seopress_social_fb_img_height":0,"_seopress_social_twitter_title":"","_seopress_social_twitter_desc":"","_seopress_social_twitter_img":"","_seopress_soc